review_comments.body:
I prefer avoiding hardcoding if those RPCs are controlled by MV.

MV can return the header version directly and `ApiKeys` can look up the API version based on the header version. With both helpers, the hardcoding can be stripped out. 
```java

public short requestHeaderVersion() {
    return isAtLeast(IBP_4_5_IV0) ? (short) 3 : (short) 2;
}

public short latestVersionForRequestHeader(short headerVersion) {
    for (short v = latestVersion(); v >= oldestVersion(); v--) {
        if (requestHeaderVersion(v) <= headerVersion) return v;
    }
    throw new UnsupportedVersionException(this + " has no version using request header v" + headerVersion + " or lower");
}

public Builder(WriteShareGroupStateRequestData data, short requestHeaderVersion) {
    super(ApiKeys.WRITE_SHARE_GROUP_STATE,
        ApiKeys.WRITE_SHARE_GROUP_STATE.oldestVersion(),
        ApiKeys.WRITE_SHARE_GROUP_STATE.latestVersionForRequestHeader(requestHeaderVersion));
    this.data = data;
}
```

